A short prompt through the same path also answers correctly:
$ HOME=... opencode run "Reply with exactly the word DIRECTSHORT and nothing else."
  DIRECTSHORT
  exit=0

READING: the provider generates 200 lines on demand. Through Podium the same
prompt produces a burst of 23 preview frames in the first 15s, then nothing:
phase stays `working`, the durable transcript stays at ZERO characters, and no
error ever arrives. Short prompts through Podium do complete and do write durable
text (the reply and attach cells pass on this harness), so this is specific to a
long turn, not to the harness being dead.

WHY THIS BLOCKS THE INTERRUPT CELL: the interrupt row's control requires the turn
to be observed IN FLIGHT immediately before the call — because interrupting
nothing always looks like success. A turn that is stalled rather than generating
cannot satisfy that, so the cell is REFUSED rather than scored. Reporting FAIL
here would be reporting that interrupt is broken on the strength of a turn that
was not running.
